-- title:
--   Igusa chart algebras as localisations with unchanged reduction mod ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and write $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $S\subseteq F$ be an arbitrary subset. For a base ring $R$ acting on $F$, both `IgusaScheme.chartAlg` and `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg` denote the subalgebra of those $x\in F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $S$, i.e. the integral closure of $R[S]$ in $F$. The assertion is threefold. First, `IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S` coincides with `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg` formed over the base $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$. Second, for $x\in F$ one has $x\in$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S` if and only if there exist $a$ in the integral closure of $\mathbf{Z}[S]$ in $F$ and an integer $s$ with $\ell\nmid s$ such that $s\,x=a$ in $F$. Third, there is an inclusion of the $\mathbf{Z}$-chart algebra into the $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$-chart algebra (every element of the former lies in the latter), together with a ring isomorphism between the quotient of the $\mathbf{Z}$-chart algebra by the ideal generated by $\ell$ and the quotient of the $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$-chart algebra by the ideal generated by $\ell$, which sends the class of $a$ to the class of $a$ viewed in the larger algebra.
--
--   This is the ring-level comparison, chart by chart, between the integral model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbf{Z}$ and the Igusa model over $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$: localisation commutes with integral closure, so the $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$-chart algebra is the localisation of the $\mathbf{Z}$-chart algebra away from $\ell$, and the two have the same reduction modulo $\ell$. It is used in the identification of the Igusa scheme with a base change of the two-chart integral model, in the construction of pinned degeneracy pairs, and in the unramifiedness statements attached to the Deligne–Rapoport model package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_chartAlg_eq_and_mem_iff_and_exists_ringEquiv_quotient_span_natCast.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open ModularCurve ModularCurve.IgusaScheme AlgebraicCurve

theorem ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.chartAlg_eq_and_mem_iff_and_exists_ringEquiv_quotient_span_natCast
    (N ℓ : ℕ) [NeZero N] [Fact ℓ.Prime] (S : Set ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N)) :
    IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S =
        TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ↥(GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ) ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S ∧
    (∀ x : ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N), x ∈ IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S ↔
        ∃ (a : ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N)) (s : ℤ), a ∈ TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S ∧
          ¬ ((ℓ : ℤ) ∣ s) ∧ (s : ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N)) * x = a) ∧
    (∃ (hle : ∀ a : ↥(TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S), (a : ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N)) ∈ IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S)
       (e : (↥(TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S) ⧸
              Ideal.span {((ℓ : ℕ) : ↥(TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S))}) ≃+*
            (↥(IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S) ⧸ Ideal.span {((ℓ : ℕ) : ↥(IgusaScheme.chartAlg N ℓ S))})),
       ∀ a : ↥(TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) S),
         e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ⟨(a : ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N)), hle a⟩) := by sorry
